<body data-lang="both">

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue? <span class="zh-title">为什么天空是蓝色的？</span></h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Three audiences · 三种读者 &nbsp;·&nbsp; English / 中文 side by side</p>
  <div class="lang-toggle">
    <button data-lang="both" class="active">Both · 双语</button>
    <button data-lang="en">English</button>
    <button data-lang="zh">中文</button>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

  <!-- ===== Toddler ===== -->
  <section class="pair">
    <div class="card en">
      <h2>🧸 For a 3-Year-Old <span class="lang-tag">EN</span></h2>
      <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's really made of all the colors of the rainbow mixed together. When the sunshine flies through the air to reach your eyes, it bumps into tiny, tiny bits of air — smaller than anything you can see!</p>
      <p>When the light bumps, the short colors (like blue) bounce around super fast, everywhere in the sky. The long colors (like red) keep flying mostly straight. So when you look up, all that bouncing blue light gets in your eyes, and the sky looks blue!</p>
      <p>That's why at sunset, the light has to travel through <em>so much</em> air to reach you — the blue bounces away before it gets there, and you get to see red and orange instead. 🌅</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card zh">
      <h2>🧸 给3岁小孩 <span class="lang-tag">中文</span></h2>
      <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但其实它是彩虹的所有颜色混在一起的。当阳光穿过空气飞到你的眼睛里时，它会撞上超超小的空气微粒——比你眼睛能看到的一切都还要小得多！</p>
      <p>光撞到它们的时候，短的颜色（比如蓝色）在天空里到处飞快地反弹。长的颜色（比如红色）则基本直直地飞过去。所以你抬头看的时候，到处反弹的蓝光全跑进了你的眼睛，天空看起来就是蓝色的！</p>
      <p>这就是为什么在日落的时候，阳光要穿过<em>好多</em>空气才能到达你的眼睛——蓝色光还没到就被弹走了，所以你看到的是红色和橙色。🌅</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== High Schooler ===== -->
  <section class="pair">
    <div class="card en">
      <h2>📚 For a High Schooler <span class="lang-tag">EN</span></h2>
      <p>The sky is blue because of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> — the way light scatters off molecules in the atmosphere.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sunlight is a mix of all visible wavelengths, but it behaves like a wave. Each molecule in the air (mostly N₂ and O₂, ~99% of the atmosphere) is much smaller than the wavelength of visible light.</li>
        <li>When an electromagnetic wave hits such a small molecule, it shakes the molecule's electrons. The molecule then re-radiates light — that's scattering.</li>
        <li>The crucial part: the scattering intensity for a single molecule is proportional to <strong>1/λ⁴</strong>. Blue light (λ ≈ 450 nm) scatters roughly <strong>(650/450)⁴ ≈ 5× more</strong> than red light (λ ≈ 650 nm).</li>
        <li>Over a path through the atmosphere, a significant fraction of the blue component gets scattered in all directions. Some of that scattered blue reaches your eyes from every part of the sky, so the sky itself glows blue rather than just the sun.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Why not violet (λ ≈ 400 nm, which scatters even more)? Three reasons:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>The Sun emits less violet light (its spectrum peaks in the visible/near-IR, not violet).</li>
        <li>Some violet light is absorbed high in the atmosphere by ozone.</li>
        <li>Your eyes are less sensitive to violet — your cones peak in the blue-green range, so our visual system reads "blue."</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Sunsets:</strong> when the Sun is low, sunlight passes through a much longer path in the atmosphere. Almost all the blue is scattered away, leaving the reddish, orange direct light — and the reds scatter <em>less</em>, so they survive the long journey.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card zh">
      <h2>📚 给高中生 <span class="lang-tag">中文</span></h2>
      <p>天空是蓝色的，这是因为<strong>瑞利散射</strong>——光在大气中的分子上散射的方式。</p>
      <ul>
        <li>阳光是所有可见波长的混合，但它像波一样传播。空气中的每个分子（主要是 N₂ 和 O₂，约占大气的 99%）都比可见光的波长小得多。</li>
        <li>当电磁波撞击这么小的分子时，它会震动分子中的电子。分子随后重新辐射光——这就是散射。</li>
        <li>关键部分：单个分子的散射强度与 <strong>1/λ⁴</strong> 成正比。蓝光（λ ≈ 450 nm）的散射比红光（λ ≈ 650 nm）多大约 <strong>(650/450)⁴ ≈ 5 倍</strong>。</li>
        <li>在穿过大气层的路径上，相当大比例的蓝色光被散射到各个方向。其中一些被散射的蓝光从天空各处进入你的眼睛，所以天空本身发着蓝光，而不只是太阳在发光。</li>
      </ul>
      <p>为什么不呈紫色（λ ≈ 400 nm，散射得更多）？三个原因：</p>
      <ol>
        <li>太阳发出的紫光较少（它的光谱峰值在可见光/近红外，不在紫区）。</li>
        <li>一些紫光在高空中被臭氧吸收。</li>
        <li>你的眼睛对紫光不敏感——你的视锥细胞峰值在蓝绿范围，所以我们的视觉系统把它读作"蓝色"。</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>日落：</strong>当太阳位置低时，阳光穿过大气的路径长得多。几乎所有的蓝光都被散射掉，只剩下偏红的、橙色的直射光——而且红光的散射<em>更少</em>，所以它们能走完这段长路。</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== PhD ===== -->
  <section class="pair">
    <div class="card en">
      <h2>🔬 For a Physics PhD <span class="lang-tag">EN</span></h2>
      <p>The observed blue is a consequence of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> by a dilute gas of neutral molecules in the molecular (optically thin) regime, where the relevant dimensionless size parameter is x = 2πr/λ ≪ 1 (for N₂, r ~ 1.5 Å, λ ~ 500 nm → x ~ 2×10⁻³), so the leading term in the Mie series dominates.</p>
      <p><strong>The cross section.</strong> For a molecule with polarizability α in a medium of relative permittivity ε, the Rayleigh differential cross section for unpolarized incident light at frequency ω = 2πc/λ is:</p>
      <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = ( k⁴ / 4πε₀² ) · ( |α|² / 2 ) · ( 1 + cos²θ )</div>
      <p>(up to the depolarization factor ρ ≈ 0.1 for air, arising from the anisotropic polarizability tensor). The total cross section scales as σ ∝ ω⁴/λ⁴ — the classic <strong>ω⁴ (or 1/λ⁴) law</strong> — which comes from treating the induced dipole as an oscillating electric dipole radiating with power ∝ ω⁴.</p>
      <p><strong>Optical depth and color.</strong> The attenuation of direct (forward) light through a path L is I(λ) = I₀(λ) e^(−τ(λ)) with τ(λ) = σ(λ)nL. For L ~ 10 km (a zenith line of sight through ~100 km of air projected), τ(450 nm) ~ 0.1 while τ(650 nm) ~ 0.02. The <em>color</em> of the scattered sky light is set by the spectral weighting of the incident solar spectrum (AM1.5 ≈ Planck at ~5800 K, modified by O₃, H₂O, and aerosols) times 1/λ⁴, integrated over solid angle. A single scattering event gives roughly a 5–6× relative enhancement of blue over red in the diffuse component.</p>
      <p><strong>Why not violet — quantitatively.</strong> The violet problem is a three-factor product:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Solar spectral flux</strong>: F_⊙(400 nm) ≈ 1.3×10⁻³ W m⁻² nm⁻¹ vs F_⊙(450 nm) ≈ 1.8×10⁻³ (≈30% less at 400 nm).</li>
        <li><strong>1/λ⁴ boost</strong>: (450/400)⁴ ≈ 1.53 — violet scatters ~50% more per photon, not enough to overcome the flux deficit.</li>
        <li><strong>Human photometry</strong>: the V(λ) photopic sensitivity curve is ~10× lower at 400 nm than at 450 nm, and the S-cone (blue) mechanism is the effective blue channel. Additionally, stratospheric O₃ (Chappuis band, τ_O₃(400 nm) ~ 0.4) absorbs a significant fraction of the near-UV/violet.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Net effect: the perceived color is a blue with a cyan tint. (In UV-dominant spectra — e.g., under a star with a much hotter effective temperature — the sky <em>would</em> appear violet.)</p>
      <p><strong>Refinements and corrections.</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Aerosol (Mie) scattering</strong>: for r ≳ λ/10, σ no longer scales as 1/λ⁴ (Mie theory; σ ≈ 2πr² × geometric cross section × efficiency Q_sca with weak wavelength dependence). This washes out the blue dominance — it's why hazy sky with high aerosol optical depth appears white-gray, and why Mars' sky is tan but glows blue around the Sun (CO₂ with micron-scale dust scattering the shorter wavelengths forward, while the direct Sun is reddened).</li>
        <li><strong>Multiple scattering</strong>: a full radiative-transfer solution (the equation of transfer) is needed for accurate sky radiance; single-scattering Rayleigh gives the color but not the angular structure. The forward-backward asymmetry (1 + cos²θ) produces the slightly brighter horizon sky.</li>
        <li><strong>Rayleigh's 1899 explanation</strong> also includes the <strong>rotational Raman (intra/intermolecular) contribution</strong> from the anisotropic part of the polarizability tensor, which gives the small depolarization and a slightly different angular dependence.</li>
        <li><strong>Why the Sun is white overhead</strong>: direct sunlight has τ ~ 0.1–0.2 attenuation (a few % of the blue), not enough to be perceptible; it only accumulates near the horizon (path length ~ 40× longer) where the reds dominate.</li>
        <li>On planets: Titan's orange sky is <strong>Tholin</strong> (aerosol) absorption dominating over Rayleigh; Venus' yellowish-white is sulfate aerosol (Mie) plus cloud opacity.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card zh">
      <h2>🔬 给物理学博士 <span class="lang-tag">中文</span></h2>
      <p>观察到的蓝色是<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的结果：稀薄的中性分子气体处于分子（光学薄）区域，其中相关的无量纲尺寸参数为 x = 2πr/λ ≪ 1（对于 N₂，r ~ 1.5 Å，λ ~ 500 nm → x ~ 2×10⁻³），因此 Mie 级数的首项占主导地位。</p>
      <p><strong>截面。</strong>对于极化率为 α 的分子，在相对介电常数为 ε 的介质中，频率为 ω = 2πc/λ 的非偏振入射光的瑞利微分截面为：</p>
      <div class="formula">dσ/dΩ = ( k⁴ / 4πε₀² ) · ( |α|² / 2 ) · ( 1 + cos²θ )</div>
      <p>（考虑空气中的去极化因子 ρ ≈ 0.1，它源于各向异性极化张量）。总截面按 σ ∝ ω⁴/λ⁴ 缩放——经典的 <strong>ω⁴（或 1/λ⁴）定律</strong>——这源于将感应偶极子视为以功率 ∝ ω⁴ 辐射的振荡电偶极子。</p>
      <p><strong>光学厚度与颜色。</strong>直射（前向）光沿路径 L 的衰减为 I(λ) = I₀(λ) e^(−τ(λ))，其中 τ(λ) = σ(λ)nL。对于 L ~ 10 km（天顶视线穿过约 100 km 空气的投影），τ(450 nm) ~ 0.1，而 τ(650 nm) ~ 0.02。散射天空光的<em>颜色</em>由入射太阳光谱（AM1.5 ≈ 5800 K 普朗克谱，经 O₃、H₂O 和气溶胶修正）的光谱加权乘以 1/λ⁴，并对立体角积分决定。单次散射事件在漫射分量中大约使蓝色相对红色增强 5–6 倍。</p>
      <p><strong>为什么不呈紫色——定量地看。</strong>紫色问题是一个三因子的乘积：</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>太阳光谱辐照度</strong>：F_⊙(400 nm) ≈ 1.3×10⁻³ W m⁻² nm⁻¹，对比 F_⊙(450 nm) ≈ 1.8×10⁻³（400 nm 处少约 30%）。</li>
        <li><strong>1/λ⁴ 增强</strong>：(450/400)⁴ ≈ 1.53——每个光子紫光散射多约 50%，不足以弥补辐照度的不足。</li>
        <li><strong>人眼光度学</strong>：V(λ) 明视觉敏感度曲线在 400 nm 处比 450 nm 处低约 10 倍，且 S 锥体（蓝光）机制是有效的蓝色通道。此外，平流层 O₃（Chappuis 带，τ_O₃(400 nm) ~ 0.4）吸收了相当一部分近紫外/紫光。</li>
      </ol>
      <p>综合效果：感知到的颜色是带青色调的蓝色。（在紫外主导的光谱下——例如在一个有效温度高得多的恒星下——天空<em>会</em>呈现紫色。）</p>
      <p><strong>细化与修正。</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>气溶胶（Mie）散射</strong>：对于 r ≳ λ/10，σ 不再按 1/λ⁴ 缩放（Mie 理论；σ ≈ 2πr² × 几何截面 × 效率因子 Q_sca，且波长依赖较弱）。这冲淡了蓝色的主导地位——这就是为什么气溶胶光学厚度高的雾霾天空呈白灰色，也为什么火星的天空呈黄褐色但在太阳周围发蓝光（CO₂ 加上微米级尘埃将较短波长前向散射，而直射的太阳光被红化）。</li>
        <li><strong>多次散射</strong>：要得到精确的天空辐射亮度，需要完整的辐射传输解（即辐射传输方程）；单次瑞利散射能给出颜色，但不能给出角向结构。前后不对称性（1 + cos²θ）使得地平线附近的天空略微更亮。</li>
        <li><strong>瑞利 1899 年的解释</strong>还包括来自极化张量各向异性部分的<strong>转动拉曼（分子内/分子间）贡献</strong>，它给出微小的去极化效应和略有不同的角向依赖关系。</li>
        <li><strong>为什么头顶的太阳是白色的</strong>：直射阳光的 τ ~ 0.1–0.2 衰减（仅百分之几的蓝色光），不足以被人感知；只有在接近地平线时（路径长度约长 40 倍），红色才会占主导。</li>
        <li>在其他行星上：土卫六（泰坦）的橙色天空是<strong>雷林（Tholin）</strong>（气溶胶）吸收主导瑞利散射的结果；金星的黄白色天空则是硫酸盐气溶胶（Mie 散射）加上云层不透明度的结果。</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer>
  Content sources: sky.md (EN) · sky2.md (中文) — no external resources; all CSS/JS inline.
</footer>

<script>
  (function () {
    var btns = document.querySelectorAll('.lang-toggle button');
    function setLang(lang) {
      document.body.dataset.lang = lang;
      btns.forEach(function (b) {
        b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.lang === lang);
      });
      try { localStorage.setItem('sky-lang', lang); } catch (e) {}
    }
    btns.forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('click', function () { setLang(b.dataset.lang); });
    });
    try {
      var saved = localStorage.getItem('sky-lang');
      if (saved && document.querySelector('.lang-toggle button[data-lang="' + saved + '"]')) {
        setLang(saved);
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>

</body>
</html>
